      description: "Returns the first key associated with `value`, or `null` when no match exists. The optional `after` argument restricts the search to entries after that key."
      example:
        - "myMap = { \"answer\": 42, \"bar\": 23, \"foo\": \"moo\" }"
        - key = myMap.indexOf(42)
        - if key != null then
        - "   print(\"Map contains the answer.\")"
        - else
